# Unity-Specific Patterns

## MonoBehaviour Setup
- Use `[Header("Section Name")]` for Inspector organization
- Cache component references in Awake() or Start()
- Use `[SerializeField]` for private fields exposed in Inspector
- Implement IManagerDebugInterface for managers when possible

## Coroutines
- Always store coroutine reference to allow stopping
- Stop coroutines in OnDestroy()
- Use `yield return null` for frame delays, `WaitForSeconds` for timed delays

## Events
- Use UnityEvent for Inspector-configurable events
- Use C# events for code-only subscriptions
- Always null-check before invoking: `OnEvent?.Invoke()`

## ScriptableObjects
- Place in `Assets/data/` directory
- Use `[CreateAssetMenu]` attribute
- Validate data in `OnValidate()` method

## Naming Conventions
- Managers: `[Function]Manager.cs` (e.g., WaveManager.cs, GridManager.cs)
- Components: Descriptive noun (e.g., Tile.cs, CubeManager.cs)
- Data: `[Type]Data.cs` (e.g., WaveData.cs, StageData.cs)
- Utilities: `[Function]Utils.cs` or `[Function]Helper.cs`
- Interfaces: `I[Capability].cs` (e.g., IManagerDebugInterface.cs)
- Inspector variables: `[SerializeField] private GameObject targetPrefab;`
- Public properties: `public bool IsActive { get; private set; }`
- Private fields: `private float currentSpeed;` (camelCase)
- Constants: `private const float MAX_SPEED = 10f;` (UPPER_CASE)

## Project Structure
- Managers: `Assets/scripts/Managers/`
- Components: `Assets/scripts/Components/`
- Data: `Assets/scripts/Data/` and `Assets/data/`
- Utils: `Assets/scripts/Utils/`
- Enumerations: `Assets/scripts/Utils/Enumerations.cs`
- Debuggers: `Assets/scripts/Debuggers/`
